WEBVTT

00:09:27.370 --> 00:09:31.127
LR: That's one of the funniest
things, it made my day.

00:09:31.151 --> 00:09:32.678
AG: That makes me wonder Lauren,

00:09:32.702 --> 00:09:35.661
do you think we should just abandon
job interviews altogether?

00:09:36.122 --> 00:09:38.035
LR: There are parts of me that say yes,

00:09:38.059 --> 00:09:40.142
but I know that no one would ever do it.

00:09:40.725 --> 00:09:43.147
AG: Scrapping brainteasers
is a good start,

00:09:43.171 --> 00:09:44.781
but even with relevant questions,

00:09:44.805 --> 00:09:47.035
one of the other big mistakes
interviewers make

00:09:47.059 --> 00:09:49.540
is asking different questions
to each candidate.

00:09:49.564 --> 00:09:52.502
That makes it impossible
to compare apples to apples.

00:09:52.526 --> 00:09:54.589
You end up trying
to contrast strawberries,

00:09:54.613 --> 00:09:56.166
bananas and grapes.

00:09:57.023 --> 00:09:59.500
The solution is a structured interview.